WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.861
Here's what you'll be able to
do by the end of this module,

2
00:00:02.861 --> 00:00:05.225
which takes about fifty
minutes with the lab.

3
00:00:05.225 --> 00:00:07.828
You'll explain the loop's
five steps and name

4
00:00:07.828 --> 00:00:10.287
the file in the kit
that performs each one.

5
00:00:10.287 --> 00:00:12.782
You'll describe the fields of the identity

6
00:00:12.782 --> 00:00:15.562
finding's data contract
and what each one is for.

7
00:00:15.562 --> 00:00:19.489
You'll validate a finding payload
on a laptop, and predict whether

8
00:00:19.489 --> 00:00:23.925
ServiceNow accepts it, rejects it or
de-duplicates it, and when it falls due.

9
00:00:23.925 --> 00:00:28.500
And you'll recognize an intended state
that gives the re-read nothing to check.

10
00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:31.928
Before you start, read
Chapter 10 of the Governance,

11
00:00:31.928 --> 00:00:35.112
Drift and Evidence book,
and skim its Appendix B.

12
00:00:35.112 --> 00:00:40.050
For Lab 1 you need Python, Node.js
and a Bash-compatible shell.

13
00:00:40.050 --> 00:00:44.450
You don't need a ServiceNow instance
or a SailPoint tenant until Lab 2.
